<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<itop_design xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" version="3.2">
  <!--
    The three classes this authorization server keeps. None of them is in the
    grant_by_profile category, so only an Administrator can read or change them
    in the console: a person manages a connection through the PersonalToken it
    owns, which authent-token already shows under My Account.

    The secrets (a client never has one, but a code and a refresh token do) are
    AttributeOneWayPassword: a salted password_hash, never a usable value, and
    an iAttributeNoGroupBy, so altioo-mcp masks them too. A secret is handed out
    as "<row key>.<secret>": the row is found by its key, and the secret checked
    against the hash.

    Fields that change on every refresh are not tracked: an hourly rotation
    would otherwise write a change record per connection per hour.
  -->
  <classes>
    <class id="AltiooOAuthClient" _delta="define">
